1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,600
(Ancient roleplay)
Where is this place?

2
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,480
(Highlights)
This is my palace.

3
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:10,680
(The closest ones hurt the most)
Still in your princess fantasy?

4
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:13,340
Kneel and shout,
"Long live the Princess!"

5
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:14,080
(Playing along)

6
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,040
Ghost soldier's armor.
The armor worn by ghost soldiers.

7
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:20,600
I thought it's ghost soldier A and B.

8
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:21,640
Have you seen this before?

9
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,800
It's a crystal.

10
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:24,940
(Immersed in the ancient role)

11
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:26,860
(What happened to you?)

12
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,300
(Come on, show us)
I thought you'd be good at this.

13
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:30,940
(Nope)

14
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:32,580
(This doesn't seem right)

15
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,280
(New role, new adventure)
Who is that?

16
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:35,280
The others.

17
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,560
They got captured too?

18
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:38,440
Of course. We all got captured together.

19
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:40,240
(Losing it)
Who changed my destination?

20
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:41,480
I didn't mean to.

21
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:42,920
But I actually...

22
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:43,340
(Confidential)

23
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:44,400
(Giving up)
Shoot me if you can.

24
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:45,980
(Someone please stop this)

25
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:46,880
I'll lead the way.

26
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:48,560
Okay.

27
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,080
Follow me.

28
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,000
I found the key evidence

29
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,840
at the very beginning.

30
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:59,940
=Truth Clubhouse=

31
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:02,260
(Ancient guests at an exhibition)

32
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:03,500
(Waiting to begin)
Hold on.

33
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,420
I'm taking you somewhere.

34
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:06,300
What are you doing?

35
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:07,980
This place...

36
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:08,780
What's going on?

37
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:09,820
What?

38
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:10,940
What did you say?

39
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:12,900
I'm Ding Tian.

40
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:15,540
The famous Ding Tian.

41
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:16,820
Ding Tian.

42
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:18,180
What's this place called?

43
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:19,620
This is Hehe.

44
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:21,140
What did you just say?

45
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:21,980
Here.

46
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:23,020
This place?

47
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:26,300
This is Tui Exhibition Hall.

48
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:29,460
I'm the security guard here.

49
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:31,700
You can call me Mr. Ding.

50
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,580
What?

51
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:33,740
Mr. Ding.

52
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:34,900
I mean Sichuan dialect.

53
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:36,180
How do you say that in Sichuanese?

54
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:37,020
Mr. Ding.

55
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:38,060
Mr. Ding...

56
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:39,700
There's someone else.

57
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:40,740
Jin's over there.

58
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:42,700
Where's Jin?

59
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:43,260
Can't you see her?

60
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:44,140
Whoa!

61
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:46,780
She's wearing all red. That's creepy.

62
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:49,020
So your character speaks Sichuanese?

63
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:51,100
Yep, that's the plan.

64
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:52,420
Is that so strange?

65
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:54,420
Can't I speak it?

66
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:55,020
Of course you can.

67
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:56,140
But if it's part of your character,

68
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,460
that's suspicious.

69
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:00,100
No, I just wanted to.

70
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:02,180
Oh, okay.

71
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:04,240
Hey,

72
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:07,240
take a look at the year.

73
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:09,750
See how it's different

74
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:11,030
from your year 260.

75
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:12,000
(Let me see)
Alright.

76
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,160
Three,

77
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:14,000
two,

78
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:14,880
one.

79
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:19,260
(Trying to scare them)

80
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:22,220
(Scare prank failed)

81
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:23,760
(Honest review)
It's pretty simple.

82
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:24,800
Shouldn't you be like...

83
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,960
(Instant roleplay)
What's this?

84
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,640
You're supposed to act surprised.

85
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:29,680
(So fascinating)
Stop acting.

86
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:30,520
Look at this.

87
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:34,240
Isn't it just a stone?

88
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:37,800
Does anyone know what this is?

89
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:39,400
Witchcraft.

90
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,020
(Makes perfect sense)

91
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,040
A glowing pearl?

92
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:42,960
(2026 version)
Exactly.

93
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,360
A glowing stick.

94
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:46,640
Where is this place?

95
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:48,040
This is a palace.

96
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:48,520
Come on.

97
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:50,840
This is my palace.

98
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:53,040
Still in your princess fantasy?

99
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,240
Kneel and shout,

100
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,820
"Long live the Princess!"

101
00:02:55,820 --> 00:02:56,940
(Playing along)

102
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:58,320
If you really ordered me to,

103
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,040
(Loyal guard)
I'd actually do it.

104
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,720
Call the ghost soldiers.

105
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,560
Ghost soldier armor.

106
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,520
The armor worn by ghost soldiers!

107
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:07,880
The armor worn by ghost soldiers.

108
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:09,440
(Ding's repeat mode)
I thought it's ghost soldier A

109
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:10,680
(Creative imagination)
and B.

110
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:14,840
Have you seen this before?

111
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:15,720
It's

112
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:16,480
a crystal.

113
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,100
(Of course I've seen it)

114
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:18,840
(When kids go quiet,)

115
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:20,160
Where?

116
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:21,220
(trouble isn't far behind)

117
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:22,060
(Ready to fight)

118
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:26,320
Mr. Ning Waver.

119
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:27,980
(Ning is confused)

120
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:30,520
Do you remember your glory days?

121
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:31,420
(I have no idea
what you're talking about)

122
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:32,360
Are you guys serious?

123
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:33,640
He's here every day.

124
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:35,060
(Here we go again)

125
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,720
He's like a different person.

126
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:39,840
(Is this Ning Waver?)
That young commander vibe

127
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,480
(Is this really Ning?)
is completely gone.

128
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,400
(Ancient folks never had this)
What kind of technology is this?

129
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:48,600
You've never seen it, right?

130
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:53,200
(Making things up)
One photo traps your soul.

131
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,680
(Pure nonsense)
Each photo steals a piece of it.

132
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:58,100
(Why am I in there?
Why does he look like me?)

133
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:59,180
(Am I really losing my soul?)

134
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:00,540
(Take hers too)

135
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:02,380
(Don't point it at me)

136
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,300
(Picks it up)

137
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:10,220
(Looking around)

138
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:12,440
(Show time)
I thought you'd be good at this.

139
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:23,660
(Let me play a tune)

140
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:24,660
(A little rusty)

141
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,720
You can't play anymore.

142
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,080
Nope.

143
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:29,940
(Good enough)

144
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:33,460
(Playing with the hairpin)

145
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,740
(That's how the trouble started)

146
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:40,500
(What do I do now?)

147
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:43,580
(Glances over)

148
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,000
My Corn Blossom Needle.

149
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:51,100
(Smile like nothing happened)

150
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:52,540
You remembered?

151
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:53,440
(Trying to jog his memory)

152
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:54,680
I snapped it.

153
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:55,980
(Like this?)

154
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:59,020
(In-car detective drama,
full actor mode)

155
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:01,220
(Slams it down)

156
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,440
What's wrong?

157
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:05,040
(Having fun acting)
Why are you so mad?

158
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,840
I'm going to...

159
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:08,840
(Going full detective mode)
to furiously deduce this!

160
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,920
Delete your own evidence first.

161
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:14,180
(Where's my detective dignity?)

162
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:16,360
She's the detective.

163
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:17,600
Who's the detective?

164
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:18,680
Yang Glory.

165
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,320
And you?

166
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:19,840
Me too.

167
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,200
We're both detectives.

168
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:23,040
I'm the only confirmed good guy.

169
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:24,760
That's all I can say.

170
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:25,360
Got it?

171
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:27,500
I can be the third.

172
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:28,520
(Junior detective)
Junior detective.

173
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:30,100
(Thrilled on the inside)

174
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:32,680
I'm worried I'll be the killer again.

175
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:34,280
Last time was a disaster.

176
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:35,640
A total disaster.

177
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:36,600
I hid all season.

178
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:38,840
Then Ning and I were both killers.

179
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:41,320
When I called Ning,

180
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,760
I was bragging.

181
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:44,460
(Flashback)

182
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:47,120
I told him, we've got this, Ning.

183
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:51,240
(Celebrating too soon)
This time, with the two geniuses...

184
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,460
(More details in The Truth! X Episode 9)

185
00:05:52,460 --> 00:05:53,340
(If we don't get zero votes, we lose)

186
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:54,860
(No zero votes, no Golden Key)

187
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:56,480
And then?

188
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,160
Everyone voted for us.

189
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:58,200
(Culprit identified)
They got caught.

190
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:01,240
(Curious)
How'd that happen?

191
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,720
(Not one person was on my side)
Everyone voted for me.

192
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:04,000
That's so embarrassing.

193
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
You looked guilty.

194
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,720
I used to fool them.

195
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,800
(The trick failed)
Now they know me too well.

196
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:10,320
So what about Ning?

197
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:12,520
Ning was carried by me.

198
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:13,160
You know that.

199
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:15,260
(Can't hold back a laugh)

200
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:17,440
But sometimes

201
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:18,600
Ning gets a little nervous

202
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:19,700
when he lies.

203
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:20,400
(Got it)

204
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,720
Where are you going after this?

205
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:24,280
Back to Beijing.

206
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:25,640
Taking a break?

207
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:26,240
No.

208
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,640
Straight to the new drama.

209
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:29,320
(Can't wait for Zhou's new role)
He's playing the sweet boy again.

210
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,960
He's perfect for it.

211
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,840
I told him he's perfect for these roles.

212
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:34,440
Like younger boyfriend roles,

213
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,840
(Trying not to smile)
or the loyal type.

214
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:37,920
He said, "I'm gonna own this lane."

215
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:40,120
(Embarrassed)
I said, "That's the spirit."

216
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,680
He has that loyal vibe.

217
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:42,080
You know.

218
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:42,740
(Loyal)

219
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,440
(I agree)
Exactly.

220
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:45,440
That sounded forced.

221
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,120
No, no.

222
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:46,960
No, princess.

223
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:52,680
He really nailed it

224
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:53,720
yesterday.

225
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:55,160
He stayed in character the whole time.

226
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:56,920
(Deep in character mode)
I thought the whole setup was great.

227
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:58,620
(Secretly loving it)

228
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,320
So Ning

229
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:01,920
is riding with us too?

230
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,320
Yeah, there'll be
one more person in our car.

231
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:04,320
Wait,

232
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:06,000
I need to move forward.

233
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,520
Ning has long legs.

234
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:08,540
(Long legs coming aboard)
It's fine. I'll sit in the back.

235
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:09,400
(Considerate Ding)

236
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,960
My legs are shorter.

237
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:13,360
I mean there's no room in the back.

238
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,160
Watch your head.

239
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:15,240
(Considerate Hehe)
Okay.

240
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,240
I can.

241
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:17,880
If I'm right about it,

242
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:20,040
holding guns and doing illegal stuff.

243
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,480
They must be some dark organization.

244
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:22,960
I

245
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:25,040
(Not scared at all)
never back down from this.

246
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:26,040
(Go after him, not me)
Boss, get him.

247
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,000
He's the one who said it.

248
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,520
But I have a question,

249
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:31,040
guys.

250
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:31,320
What?

251
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,720
Why did we change into these clothes?

252
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:35,520
These are our original uniforms.

253
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,840
Why are you dressed like this?

254
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:37,600
(Starting to question)

255
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,160
They made me change.

256
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:39,360
No, wait.

257
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:41,200
It's not weird that we have this outfit.

258
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:41,640
Right.

259
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:42,280
You...

260
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:42,640
Yeah.

261
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:43,200
You two...

262
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,400
(Out of uniform)
Yeah, why are we...

263
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:46,000
What kind of material is this?

264
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,480
What is he making us to do?

265
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:48,160
What kind of clothes are these?

266
00:07:48,180 --> 00:07:49,940
(Amused by his own joke)

267
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:52,000
I have a question.

268
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,400
(Curious investigation)
Yesterday, Ning Bo came

269
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:56,480
from that place you mentioned,

270
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:57,400
right?

271
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,000
Do you know him?

272
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,120
He's our boss.

273
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:00,880
Yeah.

274
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:02,840
You should remember him the most.

275
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:03,840
Me?

276
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:04,160
Yeah.

277
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,160
He and you...

278
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,160
You two were married, right?

279
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:08,680
(Actually, no)
Not exactly.

280
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:10,240
His exact words were

281
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:12,440
(Joking)
he'd be very interested in you.

282
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:13,560
Interested in me?

283
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:13,840
Yeah.

284
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,160
(I'm interested too)
Okay, I like this.

285
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:17,120
(Out of choice)
Back in your era,

286
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:17,880
did anyone

287
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:19,960
really admire me?

288
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:20,320
Yes.

289
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:21,520
Admire me?

290
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,920
Want me?

291
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:25,080
(Quietly laughing)
But they could never have me.

292
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:25,400
Okay.

293
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,200
I'll pay special attention to him.

294
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,920
Actually, at your exhibition,
there's someone

295
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:30,440
named Hehe.

296
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:33,150
He also really wants to get me?

297
00:08:33,150 --> 00:08:35,150
(Going along with it)
He really wants you.

298
00:08:35,150 --> 00:08:36,150
Really?

299
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:37,030
(Feeling great)
Yeah.

300
00:08:37,030 --> 00:08:38,400
This...

301
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:39,860
(Can't stop laughing)

302
00:08:40,030 --> 00:08:41,360
What do you think of me?

303
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:43,030
(And you?)
I'm extremely loyal to you.

304
00:08:43,030 --> 00:08:44,240
You're Her Highness the Princess.

305
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:46,520
We used to be from the same kingdom.

306
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:47,880
I see.

307
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:48,840
Take me back with you, okay?

308
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,160
Because in 2026,

309
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:52,120
I don't get this kind of treatment.

310
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:55,480
We're investigating across time.

311
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:57,920
(Serious analysis)
I think they're some kind of bandits.

312
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:00,640
You're from the Touch Today Group,
right?

313
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:01,920
I have a question.

314
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:03,480
Is Ding Tian your boss?

315
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:05,000
He's the leader
of the Touch Today Group.

316
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:05,960
(Immediately questioning)
Then what are you two?

317
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:06,720
Second and third in command?

318
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:07,820
Behave yourselves.

319
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:08,560
(Seriously in character)

320
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:09,960
Stop joking.

321
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:11,400
What's wrong?

322
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:13,840
(A song for him)
My touch...

323
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:15,440
(Gentle comeback)
What's wrong?

324
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:17,700
I'm behaving perfectly.

325
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:18,680
(Acting cute)

326
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:19,400
Hey, man.

327
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,320
What's that thing in your hand?

328
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,660
(I'm new here. I don't know much)
Isn't it obvious?

329
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:23,480
What...

330
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:23,880
what is it?

331
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:24,080
What?

332
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:24,960
(Going straight for it)
Grab it!

333
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:29,560
Buddy, let's go.

334
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:30,320
Where?

335
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,760
Where are we going?

336
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:33,480
(Starting to fake being sick)
I don't feel well.

337
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:34,400
Buddy,

338
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:35,840
follow that car ahead.

339
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:36,840
Follow them.

340
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:39,080
What's wrong with you?

341
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:41,000
(Fully immersed)
Just follow me.

342
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:41,520
Alright.

343
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:44,200
(Just you wait)
Keep that attitude.

344
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,560
I'll tie you up once we get out.

345
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:46,680
Just you wait.

346
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:48,360
Who's in front?

347
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:49,600
The others.

348
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:50,840
They got tied up too?

349
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:51,200
Of course.

350
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,520
(No one escaped?)
We all got captured together.

351
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:53,920
Stop asking so many questions.

352
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,960
Why are there so many questions?

353
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:56,720
Calm down.

354
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:57,280
Just you wait.

355
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:58,800
Soon you'll tie us up

356
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:00,560
and lead us into the darkness.

357
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:01,440
How about that?

358
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,360
No need.

359
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:03,320
(Losing his spotlight)
That's not necessary.

360
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:05,140
(You think I can't handle you?)

361
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,880
This whole thing is suspicious.

362
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:09,680
Yeah, it's weird.

363
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:11,400
I get why they captured you guys.

364
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:12,640
(Caught in the crossfire)
But why did they drag me into this?

365
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:15,240
They said they were coming
for the treasures,

366
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,680
so they took us too.

367
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:18,480
Yeah, I had a location.

368
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,040
(Annoyed)
Great.

369
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:21,800
You just deleted that location,
didn't you?

370
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:22,800
(You can't escape my sharp eyes)
You don't want to take us there.

371
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:25,400
Bring the treasures here.

372
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:26,680
(How could you forget?)
Seriously?

373
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:28,440
(Changing destination)
Okay, we'll navigate there.

374
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:29,240
Buddy,

375
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:31,400
follow the new location.

376
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:32,160
Boss.

377
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:35,920
The route that car took

378
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:37,200
doesn't seem to match

379
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:38,120
the route we planned.

380
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:39,200
What do we do?

381
00:10:39,340 --> 00:10:40,680
(What does this mean?)

382
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:41,840
Could there be three treasures

383
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:43,480
in that car?

384
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:44,640
No.

385
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,080
There is one treasure here.

386
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:47,920
(Treasure No. 1)
The other two treasures are in that car.

387
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:49,880
Should we follow them?

388
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:52,080
We've already lost three.

389
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:53,080
I think

390
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,960
losing two more won't hurt.

391
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:56,040
Already

392
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,040
lost three?

393
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:57,680
Should we follow them?

394
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:58,720
Follow them.

395
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:00,080
Lost three.

396
00:11:00,080 --> 00:11:00,440
Lost...

397
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,720
(Still processing)
Follow that car.

398
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:03,960
Losing two more is fine.

399
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:04,520
Two more...

400
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:05,160
No.

401
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:06,760
There were three people just now.

402
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:07,920
Those three already went inside.

403
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:09,040
Something feels wrong.

404
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:10,120
Only the two of us are left.

405
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:10,880
(Exactly)
Right.

406
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:12,400
Is that what you mean, boss?

407
00:11:12,990 --> 00:11:14,440
Right.

408
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:15,440
Okay, boss.

409
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:16,120
That's what he means.

410
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:17,360
Boss, I'm following you.

411
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,800
(Following the boss)
I heard you're a good person.

412
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:20,880
I did this for your own safety.

413
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:23,080
(Heartfelt explanation)
You need to know my good intentions.

414
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:23,960
Then what is this R?

415
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:24,720
(Here comes the question)
What does R mean?

416
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:28,480
R is a criminal organization.

417
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,200
Then what organization are you?

418
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:33,000
(A true good guy)
I'm part of the good guys.

419
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:33,920
So your organization...

420
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:35,640
(Protecting treasures)
To protect you.

421
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:37,740
(Forcing protection)

422
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:41,000
(Approaching R Corporation)
Is this R Corporation?

423
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,120
(Whispering)
How did we end up at R Corporation?

424
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,840
Ask yourself.

425
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:46,440
You brought us here.

426
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:49,340
Don't keep clicking it.

427
00:11:49,340 --> 00:11:50,320
(Professional prop for drama scene.
Do not imitate.)

428
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:51,320
Don't let it go off, Ding.

429
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:52,700
(Careful reminder)

430
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:54,280
Unbelievable.

431
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,060
(Frustrated)

432
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:56,660
(Keeping quiet)

433
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:58,360
Boss,

434
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,960
these two talk too much.

435
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,320
Take off your socks.

436
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,480
(Got a great idea)
Stuff them in their mouth.

437
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:04,260
(I'll shut my mouth, Mr. Ding)

438
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:05,720
Can I delete this?

439
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:07,200
(Loudly plotting)
What if they use this against me?

440
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:07,680
What do I do?

441
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:08,400
Makes sense.

442
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,920
Wait a second.

443
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:12,520
(How dare she?) How can you do this
in front of two detectives?

444
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,040
You guys...

445
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:14,360
Oh, you guys are detectives.

446
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:14,560
No.

447
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:16,360
(She's not taking us seriously)
Aren't you ancient people?

448
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,840
We just learned

449
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:18,480
some modern knowledge.

450
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:19,600
(Fully loaded with knowledge)
So don't try to fool us.

451
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,280
Right.

452
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,480
No.

453
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:22,160
Don't bully ancient people, okay?

454
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:24,480
(Confiscated)
I'll take custody of this evidence.

455
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,600
I'll find the key evidence,

456
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:27,920
(Searching carefully)
guys.

457
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:29,360
Let's check the invoice first.

458
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:31,440
It was sent to her partner,

459
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:33,440
(Your cover is blown)
Helpful Contact.

460
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:34,960
Team,

461
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:36,560
I found the key evidence

462
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:38,360
at the very beginning.

463
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:39,560
(Found it before it even began)
What a shame.

464
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:41,040
I already know who the culprit is.

465
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:43,160
We haven't even gotten

466
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:44,560
to the partner section.

467
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:46,160
And I've already found the evidence.

468
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:47,320
(You're overthinking)
Why don't you check again

469
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:48,840
the person who just sent me

470
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:50,400
the location?

471
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:51,600
Isn't this

472
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:53,200
(The answer is clear)
your inside contact?

473
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:54,920
His name is "Partner."

474
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:56,480
(Not listening)
No.

475
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:59,400
(Trust my instincts)
This person is definitely suspicious.

476
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,260
Let's keep looking.

477
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:01,440
(Working hard on the case)

478
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:02,320
Stop digging, detective.

479
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:03,600
Give me a break, okay?

480
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:05,720
This is like a boyfriend checking up
on his girlfriend.

481
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:06,980
(Imagining a romance again)
So sweet.

482
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:10,600
Just come clean.

483
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,320
(Can't resist acting)
I won't let other guys get close to you.

484
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:14,580
(Only focused on evidence)

485
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:15,940
What's your organization's name?

486
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:16,780
(Meanwhile)

487
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:19,160
(I remember now)
The Touch Today Group.

488
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:20,800
(Just remembered)
The Touch Today Group.

489
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:21,520
They all dress like

490
00:13:21,520 --> 00:13:23,280
(Instant joke review)
circus performers.

491
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:25,360
(How dare you)
How can you talk to boss like that?

492
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:26,310
(Professional prop for drama scene.
Do not imitate.)

493
00:13:26,310 --> 00:13:27,200
(I meant the second and third in command)
This one's scary.

494
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,240
This one's easy to bully.

495
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,860
(Definitely easy to bully)

496
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,480
So this is how

497
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:32,880
(Trying to annoy him)
the Touch Today Group works?

498
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:33,600
How dare you

499
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,660
question me?

500
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,480
What makes you think
you can question me?

501
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,520
You have a gun right now.

502
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:39,200
Wait.

503
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,000
Come on, fire a shot.

504
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,520
(Taunting)
Go on. Shoot.

505
00:13:41,580 --> 00:13:42,800
(Let you enjoy your moment)

506
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:43,600
Stay quiet.

507
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:44,040
Got it?

508
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,680
You're suspicious,

509
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:48,520
Jin Thrifty.

510
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:50,220
(I've got my eye on you)

511
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:51,560
Give me the phone.

512
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:53,280
(Instantly in character)
I'm deleting it.

513
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:56,200
Get out of the car.

514
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:58,520
Don't go easy on us.

515
00:13:58,520 --> 00:13:59,520
Okay?

516
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:01,040
(Stay in character)
You have to keep up the act.

517
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:02,560
Show us your boss attitude.

518
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:03,080
Right.

519
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:03,800
Yeah.

520
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,800
(Checking around)
Why did that treasure get out?

521
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,080
Who are you calling "treasure"?

522
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:12,080
Why did my guy get out too?

523
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:14,160
He made them get out.

524
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:14,940
Get out.

525
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:17,640
Hurry up.

526
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:18,900
(Cute but fierce)

527
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:22,600
Why is nobody

528
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,860
pointing a gun at me?

529
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:25,020
(Giving it a bad review)

530
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:26,640
He's into this kind of thing.

531
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:28,200
(As you wish)
Put your hands up.

532
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:30,100
(Happy. Not happy)

533
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:31,780
(Take you out)

534
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:32,320
What?

535
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:34,560
Do you think this is a game?

536
00:14:35,060 --> 00:14:36,460
(Hurry, run)

537
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:37,840
Hands up.

538
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:39,000
The two in front are still laughing.

539
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:40,660
(Obediently raises hands)

540
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,960
Stop joking.

541
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,280
What is this?

542
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:45,240
Where are we?

543
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:46,360
Stand there. Come on.

544
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,400
Stand properly.

545
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:48,040
Isn't that

546
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:49,320
the Prince of Fun's outfit?

547
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,840
(Chubby version of the Prince of Fun)

548
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:51,880
Seriously.

549
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:53,480
What are we doing?

550
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,040
Move.

551
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:57,040
Kneel down?

552
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:58,360
Move.

553
00:14:58,360 --> 00:14:59,080
Oh, move.

554
00:14:59,080 --> 00:14:59,960
(Couldn't hear clearly)
Move.

555
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:01,040
Why did you change clothes today?

556
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:02,600
Boss.

557
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:03,360
(How is it?)
Is this okay?

558
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,920
Why is he dressed like us?

559
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:06,460
(Matching outfit)

560
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:07,040
Yeah.

561
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:08,800
Did he drag us here

562
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:10,560
just to play a game?

563
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:12,400
(Completely confused)
Where is this place?

564
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:14,360
(Spots the sign)
There's an R logo.

565
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,280
Yeah.

566
00:15:15,280 --> 00:15:17,440
Why did you bring us to R Corporation?

567
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:19,520
Something's off.

568
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:20,800
Why are we here?

569
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:24,920
Ask yourself.

570
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:26,760
Where is this?

571
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:29,120
(Too scared to answer)
I don't know.

572
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:30,240
Didn't you

573
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:31,840
bring us here?

574
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:33,240
Since we're already here,

575
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:34,480
(Making the best of it)
let's check it out.

576
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,560
Let's find out what's going on.

577
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,520
Since we're already here.

578
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:38,200
I was actually

579
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:40,320
(Nervous and tongue-tied)
planning to take down their hideout.

580
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:41,000
Hideout?

581
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:41,800
Let's go.

582
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:42,800
You go take it down.

583
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:43,880
(Just here for moral support)
We'll wait outside.

584
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:44,640
After you.

585
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:45,360
(Ding Tian leads the way)
Go ahead.

586
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,520
After you.

587
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,240
(Looking for backup)
Let's go together.

588
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,080
You have...

589
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:50,560
You all have flashlights.

590
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:51,080
Yeah.

591
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:52,760
(Security essentials)
Of course.

592
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:53,800
Then there's nothing to fear.

593
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,080
(As long as the lights stay on)
What's there to be afraid of?

594
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,840
Why didn't I get a flashlight?

595
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:58,800
Neither of you have one.

596
00:15:58,800 --> 00:15:59,960
They're security guards.

597
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,840
(Security guard accent)
We're security.

598
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:02,840
So

599
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:03,880
who exactly are you?

600
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,680
Yeah.

601
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:08,600
I'm the leader of the Touch Today Group.

602
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,920
(Immediately tattling)
He almost shot me in the car.

603
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:13,520
I was protecting you.

604
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:14,360
What do you mean?

605
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:15,400
Explain yourself.

606
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:17,840
You're the three treasures.

607
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:18,760
(Treasure No. 1)
You.

608
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:19,240
(Treasure No. 2)
You.

609
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:20,920
(Treasure No. 3)
You.

610
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:23,360
Do you remember appearing
in the display window?

611
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:24,720
Yeah.

612
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:26,000
I remember.

613
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,040
R Corporation has their eyes on you.

614
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:30,160
Then I have a question.

615
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:31,400
How about the two innocent and kind,

616
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:32,800
(Fiercely hinting)
handsome and beautiful people.

617
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:33,680
Can we leave now?

618
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:34,860
No.

619
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:35,640
(Showing no mercy)

620
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:37,360
I have to protect you two as well.

621
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:39,800
I don't believe you.

622
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:41,880
Don't doubt me.

623
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:44,120
Even with a gun,
you still don't trust me?

624
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,840
That's exactly why I don't trust you.

625
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,840
Throw it in the river
and we'll believe you.

626
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:48,800
Boss,

627
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,800
why did we come here?

628
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:52,600
We changed the location.

629
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:54,960
(Losing it)
Who changed my destination?

630
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:57,160
I didn't mean to.

631
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,080
But I actually am one of the treasures.

632
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,280
(Giving up)
Shoot me if you can.

633
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:02,220
(Ah!)

634
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:04,070
Right, we...

635
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:05,980
(Bring it on)

636
00:17:06,070 --> 00:17:07,760
We suggested coming here

637
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:09,640
to investigate R Corporation

638
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:10,680
and see what's going on.

639
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:12,720
(Do you even respect me?)
Without my permission as the kidnapper?

640
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:14,350
But we voted in the car.

641
00:17:14,350 --> 00:17:15,560
Majority rules.

642
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:17,400
(Fair, just, and transparent)
Actually, your loyal follower

643
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:18,720
was strongly against it.

644
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:20,200
He was...

645
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:22,880
How could you

646
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:25,800
be swayed by their looks?

647
00:17:26,140 --> 00:17:27,300
(What a solid excuse)

648
00:17:27,310 --> 00:17:28,680
Our looks.

649
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:31,440
(I can't help it)
They all raised their hands.

650
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:31,960
Yeah.

651
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:32,920
(Jumps in to agree)
Yeah.

652
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:34,680
Majority rules.

653
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:36,280
(The easiest boss to deal with)
Fine, let's go check it out.

654
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:36,840
Okay.

655
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:37,620
You lead the way.

656
00:17:37,620 --> 00:17:38,460
(After you)

657
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:40,240
Thanks, Mr. Ding.

658
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:41,440
(Okay)
I'll lead.

659
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:42,960
Okay.

660
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:45,880
(Let's go)
Follow me.

661
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:48,920
I want to see what happens

662
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:51,160
when these lights go out.

663
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:54,200
I'll take one step back.

664
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,760
(Talk big first)
One step back.

665
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:57,820
(Then takes a huge step back)

666
00:17:57,820 --> 00:17:59,060
(And then, boss?)

667
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:02,460
(What's wrong, boss?)

668
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:04,020
(Battle mode activated)

669
00:18:06,180 --> 00:18:07,100
(What an eye-opener)

670
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:10,980
(A new organization is born)

671
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:13,040
So only three people
are going down to rescue them?

672
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:14,560
(Let's be fair)
Let's do rock-paper-scissors.

673
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,880
I think it's unfair

674
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,480
whoever goes or doesn't go.

675
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:19,120
Because we're all here to save them.

676
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:20,360
I can stay behind.

677
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:21,000
(Ready to compromise)
I can.

678
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:21,320
Exactly.

679
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:23,520
I really don't care
what people think of me.

680
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:25,640
(You can't trick me)
Say whatever you want.

681
00:18:27,320 --> 00:18:29,800
Back in my time,

682
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:31,280
there was a story

683
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:32,860
where two women rescued

684
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:35,640
(Setting up the story)
four men in danger.

685
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:37,400
I've heard that story.

686
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,440
Later, a group of men

687
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:41,240
came out and stopped them.

688
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:42,400
(This won't work on me)
Saying it wasn't appropriate.

689
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:42,920
They stopped them.

690
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:43,840
But

691
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,320
times have changed.

692
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:48,320
(Feeling inspired)
2026 belongs to you!

693
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:50,560
Exactly.

694
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:52,280
So this time,

695
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:54,080
the mission of rescuing the villagers

696
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:56,560
(Judgment made happily)
will be left to you two.

697
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:58,240
I'll take on the mission.

698
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,840
But we're supposed
to split into teams of three.

699
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:01,640
Considering

700
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,680
how good we look together,

701
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:05,040
let's think about it.

702
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:05,960
(Joining immediately)

703
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:06,360
Yeah.

704
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:07,360
Right.

705
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:09,200
(Recruiting Ding)
Because we look better together.

706
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:10,080
Wait.

707
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,320
Alright, okay.

708
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:12,120
That's right.

709
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:12,800
(Beauty is our strength)
Here's the situation.

710
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:16,160
So the three of us
will enter the password.

711
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:17,280
That's right.

712
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:18,560
They're fast runners.

713
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:20,680
We three are loud.

714
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:21,960
Two heroines,

715
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,760
plus one determined young man.

716
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:24,720
This story

717
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,680
(Main character energy)
is perfect.

718
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,400
You expect me to save them like this?

719
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:30,520
Pick someone else.

720
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:31,320
Wait.

721
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:32,560
Our team is formed.

722
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:35,120
We're called
Beauty, Strength, and Tragedy.

723
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:39,280
I asked Ding,

724
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:39,880
"How is it?"

725
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:40,480
"What's going on outside?"

726
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:41,880
He said okay.

727
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:43,160
But actually...

728
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:44,580
(Not okay)

729
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:46,360
He's always "okay."

730
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:48,000
Always saying it's okay.

731
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,200
When someone asked, "Do you need help?"

732
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:51,720
(Always okay)
No need. I'm okay.

733
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:53,000
Can we go now?

734
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:55,560
Then it's decided.

735
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:57,200
I think this works.

736
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,760
This team setup actually makes sense.

737
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:00,280
Are they really letting us go down?

738
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:02,600
(I can't believe it)
I can't believe it.

739
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:04,040
Is this show really this real?

740
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:04,880
I think we should switch someone else.

741
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:06,200
Because honestly, I've already

742
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:07,320
(Discussing)
become much braver.

743
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:08,320
I suggest...

744
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:09,720
maybe you should go.

745
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:10,960
You can cover for them a little.

746
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:11,200
Really.

747
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,640
I think it'd be pointless if he goes.

748
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:15,840
It should be fine.

749
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:17,240
It's not scary.

750
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:17,920
No.

751
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:18,920
We can't make a sound.

752
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:19,160
Right.

753
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:20,560
What's my weakness?

754
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:22,440
(The loud screamer)
I'm the loud screamer.

755
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:24,280
So being in this harsh environment

756
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:25,080
will help you grow.

757
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:26,600
Right.

758
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:28,060
(Persuaded)

759
00:20:28,100 --> 00:20:30,380
(Six people unite
for the water battle)

760
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:32,320
Are you scared up there?

761
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:34,040
(Just making things up)
We defeated a hundred people up there.

762
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:34,840
One against a hundred.

763
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:35,880
(Speaking of that...)

764
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:38,400
(Your adventures make the best stories)
I got knocked out by one hit.

765
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:40,340
The I said,
"No way, Thousand-Faced Eagle King!"

766
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:40,960
(Vivid reenactment)

767
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:42,600
I got back up.

768
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:43,480
In the end,

769
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:44,040
Ning...

770
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:44,520
Ning and I...

771
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:45,840
I said, "Ning, hurry!
Give me your hand!"

772
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:48,160
Ning said, "Go! Hurry!"

773
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:50,280
I said, "Ning, no!"

774
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:55,540
(Happy water fight moment)

775
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:56,840
We are like

776
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:58,160
holding weapons,

777
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,360
(Setting up formation)
ready to charge into a battlefield.

778
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,720
We're all going to become memes later.

779
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:01,640
Right.

780
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:02,500
This one looks cool.

781
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:03,260
(Ke likes it)
Okay.

782
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:04,840
A Gatling gun.

783
00:21:05,300 --> 00:21:06,300
(Hehe likes it)

784
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:08,320
(Getting ready)
Come, move to the back.

785
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:09,680
Coming.

786
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:10,760
Come on, we'll use shields.

787
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:11,560
The three of us
with shields go in front.

788
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,040
Okay.

789
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:13,520
We are the shields.

790
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:14,760
We fire two shots, then crouch.

791
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:15,400
You guys move forward.

792
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:16,160
Okay.

793
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:16,720
Let's go.

794
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:19,600
One, two, three.

795
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:20,160
Go.

796
00:21:32,900 --> 00:21:33,600
Push forward.

797
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:34,660
(Charge!)

798
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:35,600
Go.

799
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:36,240
Let's go.

800
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:39,120
Attack!

801
00:21:42,860 --> 00:21:43,780
(Too invested)

802
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:47,280
Careful! Watch out!

803
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:48,100
Sorry.

804
00:21:48,100 --> 00:21:48,820
(Too excited)

805
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:49,540
Are you okay.

806
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:50,380
(Concerned)

807
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:51,640
It's okay.

808
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:52,920
Alright.

809
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:54,400
We destroyed them.

810
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:57,120
(Skills incomplete, retreat)
We're fine, but they're not.

811
00:21:57,120 --> 00:21:59,280
They never expected us to use this move.

812
00:21:59,280 --> 00:21:59,720
We're doomed.

813
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:00,740
(Too much)

814
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:04,260
Don't move!

815
00:22:04,260 --> 00:22:04,800
(Put your hands up)

816
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:05,780
You don't even have a gun.

817
00:22:05,780 --> 00:22:06,500
(Out of weapons)

818
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:08,080
How do you not have a gun?

819
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:09,880
(Only defense, no offense)
You only upgraded your defense.

820
00:22:10,860 --> 00:22:12,620
(Not satisfied, water the trees)

821
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:15,360
Shield.

822
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:17,080
(Shield attacks)

823
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:18,320
The two of us combined into one shield.

824
00:22:18,320 --> 00:22:19,260
Let's fight directly.

825
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:20,340
(Shield fusion)

826
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:25,320
Jin.

827
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:27,360
Oh, Jin.

828
00:22:27,740 --> 00:22:28,820
(Justice served)

829
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:29,660
Sorry.

830
00:22:29,660 --> 00:22:31,180
(Admitting defeat)

831
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:33,800
We completed the mission, right?

832
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:35,240
This mission should count as...

833
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:35,640
No.

834
00:22:35,640 --> 00:22:36,960
(You're overthinking it)
We only escaped.

835
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:38,600
But we rescued them.

836
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:38,960
Right.

837
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:40,800
And we took down
so many R Organization members.

838
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:41,640
Not exactly.

839
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:42,560
We just put them to sleep.

840
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:43,230
(Only put them to sleep)
Are you trying to...

841
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:43,920
Everyone,

842
00:22:45,080 --> 00:22:46,200
your car is waiting outside.

843
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:46,880
Come with me. Hurry.

844
00:22:46,880 --> 00:22:47,120
Let's go.

845
00:22:47,120 --> 00:22:48,320
Okay, coming.

846
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,440
Go.

847
00:22:49,460 --> 00:22:51,740
(Being sincere
is always the ultimate weapon)

848
00:22:52,040 --> 00:22:54,160
If I were part of the production team,

849
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:56,680
(Director Jin is back)
when I invite guests next time,

850
00:22:56,680 --> 00:22:57,920
I'd make sure

851
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:58,920
they never know

852
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:01,040
that they're actually the "killer."

853
00:23:01,040 --> 00:23:02,840
That would be impressive. Yeah.

854
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:04,320
But I think it'd be really hard.

855
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:05,800
Because the killer has information.

856
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:06,840
If they follow our reasoning,

857
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:08,120
they'll definitely figure it out.

858
00:23:10,140 --> 00:23:12,220
(Almost tripped)

859
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:12,720
Yue,

860
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:15,280
why don't you
tuck your pants into your shoes?

861
00:23:16,100 --> 00:23:17,660
(He appears)

862
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:23,780
(Staring)

863
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:26,760
So you're targeting me today, huh?

864
00:23:26,760 --> 00:23:28,320
Today, I'll show you

865
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:30,280
(Intellectual attraction)
what intellectual attraction means.

866
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:31,480
You should show him

867
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:33,360
(Sharp tongue continues)
what true intellectual attraction is.

868
00:23:33,940 --> 00:23:35,420
(Such a sweet talker)

869
00:23:38,180 --> 00:23:40,660
(Director explains the next steps)

870
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:42,000
They don't even care

871
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,480
(Full firepower)
if we hear them.

872
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:45,160
I'll never confess.

873
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:46,360
Don't give anything away.

874
00:23:47,640 --> 00:23:48,720
Vote for me.

875
00:23:48,720 --> 00:23:49,960
(Provoking)
You have to vote for me.

876
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:53,160
Put pressure on me.

877
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:54,240
(Pressure is on)
Vote for me.

878
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:55,600
Okay.

879
00:23:56,280 --> 00:23:57,720
He, you're trying too hard today.

880
00:23:57,720 --> 00:23:58,240
Definitely.

881
00:23:58,240 --> 00:23:59,440
You're not usually like this.

882
00:23:59,440 --> 00:24:00,640
(Something's off)
You're acting strange today.

883
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:01,480
Right.

884
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:02,800
Trust me.

885
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:03,280
Trust you for what?

886
00:24:03,280 --> 00:24:04,720
Trust me.

887
00:24:04,720 --> 00:24:06,600
Trust that I'm a good person.

888
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:08,280
(Sincere eyes)
My eyes never lie.

889
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:09,000
He's said that before.

890
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:10,520
He's fooled us many times.

891
00:24:10,520 --> 00:24:11,280
So what do we do?

892
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:12,520
(No clue)
Give us a hint.

893
00:24:12,520 --> 00:24:14,080
He's really good at playing the killer.

894
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:16,600
So honestly,

895
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:17,680
I find it hard to vote.

896
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:19,760
Analyze it again.

897
00:24:19,760 --> 00:24:22,200
Most likely, I'd vote for Ning.

898
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,640
But

899
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:25,080
you should trust

900
00:24:25,080 --> 00:24:27,400
your own judgment more.

901
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:28,800
Just think about it yourself,

902
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:31,800
(Follow your gut)
and vote based on your instincts.

903
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:33,160
I don't care if I win or lose.

904
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:35,080
It doesn't matter to me.

905
00:24:35,080 --> 00:24:36,360
I've been fooled by He

906
00:24:36,360 --> 00:24:37,640
many times before.

907
00:24:37,640 --> 00:24:39,040
(Experienced victim)
But I don't know him well.

908
00:24:39,040 --> 00:24:40,480
But using reverse thinking...

909
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:41,200
I know him so well.

910
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:41,960
I've known him for years,

911
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:43,480
and he can still fool me.

912
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:43,960
Really?

913
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:45,000
Exactly.

914
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:46,120
So it's unpredictable?

915
00:24:46,120 --> 00:24:46,440
Yes.

916
00:24:46,580 --> 00:24:48,620
(Awaiting the reveal)

917
00:24:52,620 --> 00:24:54,820
(Hide and seek)

918
00:24:55,880 --> 00:24:57,160
Let's scare Chaoyue.

919
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:57,680
Let's go inside.

920
00:24:58,100 --> 00:24:59,740
(I didn't vote for you, Ning)

921
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:02,380
Let's scare her.

922
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:04,240
(Ke wants to play too)

923
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:05,800
(He wants to play too)
But I can see your shadow inside.

924
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:07,160
Really? You can see it?

925
00:25:07,160 --> 00:25:08,900
(Crystal clear)

926
00:25:10,160 --> 00:25:11,480
Don't get too close.

927
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:11,920
Move back.

928
00:25:12,140 --> 00:25:14,420
(His height gives it away)

929
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:18,000
Forget it.

930
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:18,600
Don't bother.

931
00:25:22,040 --> 00:25:23,400
(Next Episode Preview)
How tall are you?

932
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,200
Six foot three.

933
00:25:24,300 --> 00:25:25,780
(A full six foot three)

934
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:28,120
I look like a figure next to him.

935
00:25:28,120 --> 00:25:29,480
(Hard to believe)
How is he so tall?

936
00:25:29,900 --> 00:25:31,660
(Instant height boost)

937
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:33,440
(Deep in character. Are you ready?)
I'm wondering

938
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:34,840
will the audience even believe this?

939
00:25:34,840 --> 00:25:36,400
Even I think it's kind of scary.

940
00:25:36,460 --> 00:25:37,880
(Even he got scared)

941
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:39,120
Your wolf is kind of cute.

942
00:25:39,120 --> 00:25:40,880
(He's question)
Can you control your pack?

943
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:42,080
I'm speechless.

944
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:43,760
(I'm speechless. Mickey Mouse version)
What kind of performance is this?

945
00:25:44,520 --> 00:25:46,560
(The girls meet)
Ms. Zhang Ruonan.

946
00:25:47,520 --> 00:25:50,000
(Fully immersed)
We have to stay in character.

947
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:51,120
(Not exaggerating at all)
Seriously.

948
00:25:51,120 --> 00:25:53,040
Alright, anything else to confess?

949
00:25:53,040 --> 00:25:53,640
Listen,

950
00:25:53,640 --> 00:25:54,560
during the game,

951
00:25:54,560 --> 00:25:55,480
you can follow anyone,

952
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:56,560
just don't follow her.

953
00:25:56,720 --> 00:25:57,240
If you follow her,

954
00:25:57,240 --> 00:25:58,800
(Fear level doubles)
you'll be twice as scared.

955
00:25:59,040 --> 00:25:59,840
I'm not scared.

956
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:01,040
Really?

957
00:26:01,120 --> 00:26:02,100
I'm terrible, but I love playing anyway.

958
00:26:02,100 --> 00:26:02,540
(Addicted anyway)

959
00:26:02,580 --> 00:26:03,920
(A solo mission begins)

960
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:05,520
Please, pray for me.

961
00:26:06,520 --> 00:26:08,240
(Praying hard)
It's okay. You'll be fine.

962
00:26:10,280 --> 00:26:11,080
I can't understand

963
00:26:11,080 --> 00:26:12,240
a single word he's saying.

964
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:12,780
(Master of mishearing)

965
00:26:13,320 --> 00:26:15,640
Oh no! A solo mission.

966
00:26:16,400 --> 00:26:17,560
Why is no one talking?

967
00:26:17,580 --> 00:26:18,220
(Something feels very off)

968
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:23,040
What are you pretending?

969
00:26:23,880 --> 00:26:25,920
I thought you were gone.

970
00:26:26,500 --> 00:27:08,460
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(Viewing Calendar)

971
00:27:25,200 --> 00:27:29,200
♪Come now, players all,
let the game of reason start♪

972
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:33,640
♪Unlock each hidden trial,
let courage spark the dark♪

973
00:27:35,660 --> 00:27:39,820
♪Night falls slow, shadows grow,
the sleuth is lost inside the maze♪

974
00:27:39,820 --> 00:27:44,040
♪Figures pass, lanterns sparse,
dark currents drift without a trace♪

975
00:27:44,040 --> 00:27:47,810
♪Wind picks up, footsteps rush,
cold laughter swallowed by the dark♪

976
00:27:47,810 --> 00:27:51,920
♪Truth concealed, the night
stands still, and nothing leaves a mark♪

977
00:27:52,100 --> 00:27:56,220
♪An unsigned letter, coded words,
the solvers gather one by one♪

978
00:27:56,220 --> 00:28:00,330
♪A broken game, illusion reigns,
who's hiding what they've done?♪

979
00:28:00,330 --> 00:28:03,970
♪Hushed voices, nerves on edge,
wrapped in smoke and mirrors still♪

980
00:28:03,970 --> 00:28:06,100
♪The next second, deeper riddles,
or the answer to the kill♪

981
00:28:06,100 --> 00:28:10,050
♪Every piece of truth
has finally come to light♪

982
00:28:10,290 --> 00:28:14,210
♪Unlock the mystery, turn the question,
let's begin tonight♪

983
00:28:14,420 --> 00:28:18,570
♪Side by side, no holding back,
follow every clue to find the truth♪

984
00:28:18,570 --> 00:28:22,130
♪The story blurs like flowers in fog,
let's begin tonight♪

985
00:28:22,390 --> 00:28:27,040
♪Search for the vanished cipher,
trace the proof, and face the sleuth♪
